[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: What the operator need not judge now is filed where it resurfaces, not narrated

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: INV-FILE-DO-NOT-NARRATE
TITLE: What the operator need not judge now is filed where it resurfaces, not narrated
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Whatever the operator does not need to judge NOW is FILED, not narrated. The
contributor makes the best-educated call on how to record it and places it
where it will resurface at the right time: a backlog register node, an open
DECISION carrying a RETIRES_ON, or a NOTES paragraph on the node it affects.

Session output carries only what changes a decision in front of the operator
or blocks the work in hand. Everything in the class of "one more thing you
should know" is logged and left unspoken.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A logged finding is not lost; mentioning it costs attention, logging it costs
nothing. Filing also forces the contributor to decide WHERE a thing resurfaces,
which is the part narration skips -- a thing said in passing has no trigger
and is therefore forgotten, not deferred.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Recorded 2026-08-28 at the operator's request, as one of four contributor-communication requirements (INV-DECISIONS-ARRIVE-AS-CARDS, INV-LISTS-WHERE-THE-READER-UNPACKS, INV-FILE-DO-NOT-NARRATE, INV-SETTLED-STAYS-VISIBLE). The rule is the operator's; AUTHORED_BY reads llm because the writer has no flag for the other value. An INVARIANT is read as a REQUIREMENT under DEC-INVARIANT-IS-A-REQUIREMENT; the grammar type is kept so the grid is not half-applied. The sdoc skill's backlog protocol is the procedure these four are the requirement for.

Retyped from INVARIANT to REQUIREMENT on 2026-08-30 (DEC-INVARIANT-IS-A-REQUIREMENT; DEC-NODE-FAMILIES). The UID keeps its retired prefix: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE.
<<<
